%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%Title: Paintkit -- a backdrop that varies: pkwet /Under as a procedure (issue #179)
%%BoundingBox: 0 0 640 250
%%EndComments

% Specimen for pkwet's procedural /Under (lib/paintkit.ps). pkwet grades each
% softening pass toward /Under, "the colour already on the canvas there".
% With one [r g b] that is one colour for every pass, so over a backdrop that
% changes where the mark sits the outer passes are right at one end and leave
% a visibly pale or dark rim at the other.
%
%   /Under { y-sky }   a procedure  x y -> r g b  in the user space pkwet is
%   /At [x y]          called in, asked once per softening pass for the
%                      backdrop at /At plus that pass's displacement
%
% Left: the same cloud over the same strongly graded sky, /Under one colour
% (the sky at the cloud's centre, which is what you would hand-match): the
% passes displaced down are a cold grey against the warm horizon, where the
% gradient is furthest from the mid-sky colour; the rim above is smaller.
% Right: /Under the sky function itself. Same seed, same marks; only the
% colour each pass is mixed toward differs, and most of the rim is gone.
%
% The procedure runs inside pkwet's frame, so it must be a pure function: no
% painting, no calling pkwet, no reliance on what else is on the operand
% stack. /At is required with a procedure (pkwet cannot see where a mark
% sits) and the answer is per pass, not per pixel: a mark that is tall
% against the gradient is better split into several pkwet calls, each with
% its own /At.
%
%   pscat --page 640x250 examples/paintkit_wet_under_demo.ps --png wet_under.png

(lib/artkit.ps) run
(lib/paintkit.ps) run

/SKYTOP [0.06 0.16 0.50] def
/SKYLOW [0.98 0.86 0.68] def
/SKYH 150 def
/skyat {                                   % y -> r g b   (0 horizon .. SKYH zenith)
    SKYH div 0 max 1 min /skt exch def
    SKYLOW SKYTOP skt mix3
} def

1 1 1 setrgbcolor clippath fill

/label {                                   % x y string -
    gsave
        0.30 0.30 0.30 setrgbcolor
        /Helvetica findfont 9 scalefont setfont
        3 1 roll moveto show
    grestore
} def

% One 300 x 150 panel at (px, 50): the graded sky and the same one-colour
% cloud, softened by pkwet.
/panel {                                   % px procedural? -
    /ppro exch def /ppx exch def
    gsave
        ppx 50 translate
        newpath 0 0 moveto 300 0 lineto 300 SKYH lineto 0 SKYH lineto closepath clip
        0 1 SKYH 1 sub {
            /pgy exch def
            pgy skyat setrgbcolor
            newpath 0 pgy moveto 300 pgy lineto 300 pgy 2 add lineto 0 pgy 2 add lineto
            closepath fill
        } for
        0.99 0.98 0.97 setrgbcolor
        41 srand
        {
            newpath 50 68 moveto 100 84 150 56 215 74 curveto
            << /Nozzle 10 /Density 380 /Falloff 1 /Speck 1.1 /Overspray 0.4 >> pkspray
            newpath 75 62 moveto 130 70 170 54 235 64 curveto
            << /Nozzle 8 /Density 300 /Falloff 1 /Speck 1.1 /Overspray 0.45 >> pkspray
        }
        ppro
            { << /Soft 1 /Offset 34 /Layers 6
                 /At [ 135 70 ] /Under { exch pop skyat } >> }
            { << /Soft 1 /Offset 34 /Layers 6
                 /Under [ 70 skyat ] >> }
        ifelse
        pkwet
    grestore
} def

0   false panel
340 true  panel

10  225 (a constant /Under: one colour for every pass) label
350 225 (a procedural /Under: the backdrop where each pass sits) label
10  36 (/Under [ 70 skyat ]    the sky at the cloud's centre, hand-matched) label
10  24 (a cold grey rim below the cloud) label
350 36 (/Under { exch pop skyat }  /At [ 135 70 ]) label
350 24 (each pass mixed toward the sky at its own height: the rim is gone) label

showpage
